# Video files - now hosted on Cloudflare R2
# Keep videos locally for development, but don't commit to git
# Exception: osamasonpreview.mp4 is kept locally for homepage background
public/videos/*.mov
public/videos/*.mp4
!public/videos/osamasonpreview.mp4

# Raw client delivery (zips, duplicate media) — too large for Git; see newWork/README.md
newWork/*
!newWork/README.md
!newWork/upload-batch.txt

# ── Raw client deliveries at the repo root ──────────────────────────────────
#
# Client drops land here under names nobody can predict ("UPDATED WORK 8.22.26/",
# "NINE VICIOUS/", whatever the next artist is called), each carrying zips and
# camera masters in the hundreds of megabytes. Naming them one by one meant the
# next drop was always unprotected, and a single >100MB file caught in a commit
# makes GitHub reject the entire push — which then needs the commit rewritten.
#
# So this inverts the default: every root-level directory is ignored, and only the
# project's own directories are allowed back in. A new client folder is invisible
# to git the moment it appears, without anyone having to remember to add it.
#
# Adding a real new top-level directory to the project? Add a matching !/name/ line.
/*/
!/.claude/
!/.cursor/
!/documentation/
!/features/
!/intelligence/
!/newWork/
!/public/
!/scripts/
!/src/
!/template/

# Same reasoning for loose media dropped at the root rather than in a folder.
/*.zip
/*.mp4
/*.MP4
/*.mov
/*.MOV
